void mathlib_xplane_evaluate(RealIntercept* node, xplane_opt_t options, ...);

DESCRIPTION
The mathlib_xplane_evaluate() function processes an in-place evaluation of a 32-byte register-equivalent coordinate structure on the Exponent Plane ([X]Plane). It enforces non-commutative geometry mechanics, tracks quality chain degradation classes, handles Rule 4 boundary phase inversions, and computes Rule 9 transfinite collapse limits down to the Euclidean real axis.

Execution runs entirely on the stack or natively inside CPU registers (RAX, RDX, RCX) without dynamic memory allocation (malloc), ensuring predictable bounded latency.

ARGUMENTS
* node: Pointer to a mutable RealIntercept structure representing the working register state.
* options: Bitwise configuration flags of type xplane_opt_t altering runtime logic routing.
* ...: Variadic parameter stream used for dynamic onboarding. Accepts a secondary custom tensor component (t2), followed by sequentially accumulated register tracking overrides, terminated by XPLANE_OMIT_PARAM.

HARDWARE BIT STRUCTURE (RDX REGISTER MAPPING)
The node->Flags component maps directly to the hardware RDX control register layout:

* Bits 0–3: Scalar Shear Count (Odometer). Explicitly traps out on the 9th rollover boundary.
* Bits 4: Reserved / Alignment Buffer.
* Bits 5–14: (i) Flag Count Accumulator. Tracks negative real axis exponent crossings (Winding index).
* Bits 15–26: Multi-Shear Crossing Tracker. Tracks non-dyadic Rule 7 p-adic grid deformations.
* Bits 27–28: Exit Multiplicity Sub-bits (Bit 27: -1 Inf Exit, Bit 28: +1 Inf Exit).
* Bits 29–30: Outbound Rotations of Infinity Matrix Vector.
* Bits 31–32: Inbound Rotations of Infinity Matrix Vector.

RUNTIME FLAGS (xplane_opt_t)
* XPLANE_RUN_DEFAULT: Standard stack mode using optimized compile-time unrolled binary search loops.
* XPLANE_OPT_ACCURACY: Bypasses the strict 9th rollover shear hard crash fallback by using a 128-bit wider emulation logic loop instead of cutting off execution.
* XPLANE_NO_POOLING: Euclidean bypass mode. Drops transfinite asymptotic residue pooling, safely setting the scalar output back to zero.
* XPLANE_DISCARD_RESIDUE: Abstract tangent mode. Drops internal data fragments and extracts raw values directly from the transfinite Imaginary vector axis.
* XPLANE_OPT_EXIT_INF_NEG: Forces a Rule 9 exit sequence path bound to -1 Infinity (0x10).
* XPLANE_OPT_EXIT_INF_POS: Forces a Rule 9 exit sequence path bound to +1 Infinity (0x20).

COMPONENT FALLBACKS & ERROR HANDLING

If an odometer shear validation error occurs (total shear ≥ 9) without an accuracy override flag, node->Real is mutated to XPLANE_UNINITIALIZED (0xDEADBEEFDEADBEEF) and node->Flags degrades immediately to XPLANE_MASK_QUALITY_F.

